# Ours for pose.tf2: each class as a sandbox target facing us 300 units
# away, its feet lined up with TF2's bots' (`target set all feet <deg>`,
# a snap like TF2's setang_exact plus an offset): 30 degrees left of the
# eyes as bot_teleport leaves them (`st_<c>_raw`) and 15 right after the
# scene's teleports (`st_<c>_snap`), as measured 2026-11-20 against ours
# at -45, -20, 0, 20 and 45 (the bots' spawn yaw is 30 off a multiple of
# 45, so the step rule never puts their feet on their eyes, 4c 5); the
# Engineer's Wrench idle every 0.2 s for 3.2 s (`wr_NN`); the Spy with his
# Knife and his Revolver from the front and both sides. We stand as an
# Engineer with no view model, then the camera stays (`chimera_freecam 2`)
# and our body steps out of sight.
#   ultimate_gun_game --offscreen 1024x768 +volume 0 +sandbox tf2:ctf_2fort --scene tools/tf2ref/scenes/pose.scene --out <dir>
wait_for map_loaded 6000
wait_for spawned 3000
wait 120
god
sandbox ammo on
cl_drawhud 0
fov_desired 90
r_drawviewmodel 0
rung tf2:tf_weapon_wrench
wait 2
wait_for idle 3000
# scout
chimera_freecam 0
target remove all
wait 30
setpos 0 -300 0
setang 0 90 0
wait 30
target add tf2:scout 7.62 still protect
target set all gun tf2:tf_weapon_scattergun
wait 240
target set all feet 30
gwait 1
chimera_freecam 0
wait 2
setpos 0 -300 0
setang 0 90 0
wait 30
chimera_freecam 2
wait 2
setpos 0 -700 0
wait 10
shot st_scout_raw
target set all feet -15
gwait 1
shot st_scout_snap
